# dsv41: spill v2 and KV sharding on one pair (port of the spill side of GLM 0118,
# MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold#152: in_part, the part a point records, the per-part store
# signature), and rank_wire version 2.
# - rank_wire v2: every spill command, the write-at-keep notices included, is a rank_wire op the Tracker orders
#   (kept ids; keep, share, touch and forget notices; status polls; Leader.fail names the cause on every rank; carry
#   and borrow echoes; the followers' shard stats on request, TF_DS_KV_SHARD_STATS_MS, 0 = never). 0016's untracked
#   spill notes (lanes Kind 11) are gone.
# - spill with TF_DS_KV_SHARD=1: owner-sharded stores (blocks sized by the lineage's part: each rank writes the owner
#   rows of the parts it holds, 720 B a token, beside the replicated ones), a point restores into the part it was
#   kept from, carries and moves keep the tier's pins and generations, and the planner and the tier share one Leader
#   (Lanes.rw) and one follower (PairFollower). The SpillWithKvShard refusal is gone; with both on, every rank needs
#   the identity switches, a pool of at least two windows and its own spill folder.
# - a follower opens its store on its own thread at the agreement and rank 0 waits for it while its scan makes
#   progress (the open stats set): a large store no longer fails the start at the hello's 120 s bound.
# No new switch. Either one alone is unchanged: the spill tier alone writes 0016's replicated digest, block sizes and
# frames; TF_DS_KV_SHARD alone keeps 0018's hello, now from the shared Leader.
# Measured on the pair: spill + KV sharding (engine 9983b2f, SPILL_GIB=64, pool 2,101,248) exact.py 39/39 identical,
# tools/spill_check PASS 22/0/1, two restores while decoding 2.96 s; the daily config (engine 69c4eb4) restart check
# 4/0 and resumes from disk after a restart at 95K-237K tokens in 0.76-1.71 s against 44.6-118.4 s cold (59-70x,
# every reply equal; owner reads 890 B a token, the other rank 170 B); on the rebased engine (this series' tip, with the
# display-reserve patch beside it) exact.py identical and a 38K-token restore after a restart in 0.90 s against
# 17.9 s cold. Builds on 0016 and 0018. By Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo). Apache-2.0.
